Slice 7 is built and verified, and I have a real browser render proving the colors take. Waiting for your "commit".

**What was wrong before:** nothing was overwritten. The header had no background rule at all, and the title used the primary green, which is dark enough to read as black. Those fills are Slice 7, which did not exist when you looked. I also chased one lead from the build output: Angular 22 rewrites custom properties in component styles with a namespace placeholder. The runtime replaces it with an empty string unless an app opts in through a provider, and this app does not, so tokens resolve normally.

**Browser render (headless Chrome, fresh profile, dev server on 4200), computed values:**

| Check | Desktop 1280×800 | Mobile 375×667 |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Header background | rgb(30, 61, 5), title white | same |
| Panel bar background | rgb(65, 34, 12) | same |
| Recenter button | white icon, transparent, white border | same |
| 12 map pin colors equal the 12 list pin colors | yes, all twelve match | yes |
| Selected pin | keeps its own red, path stroke is tertiary blue | same |
| Sheet on selection | n/a | stays at peek, map at zoom 15 on the pin |

Screenshots are in the scratchpad: `shots/desktop-details.png`, `shots/mobile-list.png`, `shots/mobile-details.png`.

**Tests, build, Prettier (run by me):**

