+  text-align: center;
```

**Specs:** four new cases (list title and nav label, "Parks" while loading with an id, desktop bar title per route, mobile bar order Back → heading → toggle), the not-found case also checks the body text, and the deep-link loading case now asserts focus has not moved before loading ends. No existing case changed.

**Two review notes:**

- The subagent implemented before running the specs, so there is no captured failing run for this change. The browser walk above is the behavioral check.
- I added a "Slice 8" section to PLAN.md recording these decisions. It is uncommitted and will go in the wrap-up docs commit, not in this one.

Say "commit" and I'll commit as `style(panel): title in the bar, outlined controls, centered header`, push, and move to the wrap-up: Pass C, README draft, logs, zip, handoff.
